    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d559">

                <pb facs="0648" n="636" sameAs="frus:frus1940v03/pg636"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/6789: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Engert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-11-19T15:00:00+03:25">November 19,
                            1940—3 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 20—3 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>253. My 230, October 24, noon.<anchor n="33" xml:id="d559-f1"/> Similar
                        source<anchor n="34" xml:id="d559-f2"/> now states:</p>
                <p>(1) Soviets have promised Berlin not to interfere with German and Italian
                    projects in the Balkans in return for Turkish Armenia and, <pb facs="0649"
                        n="637" xml:id="pg637"/> if the Soviets should consider it vital, portions
                    of northern Iran. See also Legation’s 248, November 14, 3 p.m.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
